/**
 * TypeScript config for `svelte-check`.
 *
 * **A separate config because `packages/app/tsconfig.json` excludes
 * `src/renderer`.** That exclusion is right for `tsc --build` — the renderer is
 * bundled by Vite and is not part of the Node-side program — but it means `tsc`
 * never reads a single `.svelte` file, and an undefined identifier in a component
 * is invisible to it. This config exists so `svelte-check` can read them.
 *
 * It is **not** part of the `tsc --build` project graph. Adding it to
 * `references` would make `tsc` try to compile `.svelte` files, which it cannot,
 * and would double-emit the renderer.
 *
 * `skipLibCheck` is on, and that is what excludes the four errors `svelte-check`
 * otherwise reports: two in `@types/three` (`GPUTexture` is not in this
 * TypeScript version's DOM lib) and two in Svelte's own `esrap` import
 * resolution. All four are third-party declaration-file defects. Without
 * `skipLibCheck` they fail the build for reasons no commit to this repo can fix,
 * and a gate that cannot go green teaches people to ignore it.
 *
 * The comment sits **above** the object rather than inside it. Both are valid JSONC
 * and both work for `tsc`, but a comment in the first key position defeats the
 * block-comment strip a test uses to read this file as JSON — and a config that
 * needs a bespoke parser to be inspected is a config that will be skipped the next
 * time it is checked.
 */
{
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "rootDir": "..",
    "noEmit": true,
    "composite": false,
    "declaration": false,
    "declarationMap": false,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": [
    "src/renderer/**/*.ts",
    "src/renderer/**/*.svelte",
    "src/ipc.ts",
    "src/errors.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": ["../../node_modules", "dist"]
}